{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_(pythagorean_theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (pythagorean theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(similar_triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (similar triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(official_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (official solution)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the sides of a triangle have lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, what is the length of the shortest altitude?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e20ec654a837979a7d300b6ac3c1027af807201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 20  \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28pythagorean_theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(pythagorean_theorem)\">Solution (pythagorean theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (pythagorean theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can notice that the triangle must be a right triangle because its side lengths are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times those of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> right triangle. We can now draw the altitude inside of the triangle, as well as the triangle itself, labeling the vertices and points.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Let the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/750437e69454780dceef74dcf6d2278b706a75ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + CD = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecc45243b1d70d4e1e9e32342238b4a5df2991d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 50 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can now use the pythagorean theorem to set up two equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae11499fecf267c12382e59df4e878e5c29217a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + h^{2} = 40^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfcfedfefa595ea63738d399a54ea5e50298813f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(50 - x)^{2} + h^{2} = 30^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the second equation from the first, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9feb53f1d1e366a279e71f2f5fc2f5db09332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} + h^{2} - (50 - x)^{2} - h^{2} = 40^{2} - 30^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc02981f14ac5ad45d7d09879ad8653c416acaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - (50 - x)^{2} = 1600 - 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8a63364647c6f996feb75626d69a03053ab698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - (2500 - 100x + x^{2} = 1600 - 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"295\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/7350c96233995d699e497b01d7087b0534fcd564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100x - 2500 = 700$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed830b4af207ba8199b7f2bf5932ebec5914b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100x = 2500 + 700 = 3200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5361e7974d96db803e913bba80f779505beb54a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 32$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>We can now plug-in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> into the first equation we had to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83bc9ccd7855f497fb4701dd2af7da617751944a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32^{2} + h^{2} = 40^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82fc091550cd6fb35adde795501e826fec795265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^{2} = 40^{2} - 32^{2} = 8 \\times 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a08ad760496e692792a007e8bf83fc86dc0b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^{2} = 576$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d51680784e9ad72c96e49afc553d6bfcc28b2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e936f4a094c313deac49273e6768caa8eea80a43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\sqrt{576} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"167\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can repeat the same steps as solution 1 until the point where we subtract both equations and get the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7f257ab8fd59fb9ec42c03136d4ba9678d0c0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - (50 - x)^{2} = 40^{2} - 30^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c617d80dc463dc4907b79f00c0ff64b97a8b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + (50 - x))(x - (50 - x)) = (40 - 30)(40 + 30)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"395\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/24023c4f5e0aaec594023b311c489a512255f92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\times (2x - 50) = 10 \\times 70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/52816486a89e5ddaf57e3b9a6bee92cf3d3ed550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 \\times (x - 25) = 100 \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd9879d0aac8d7d2aa3abeb4a6263417683dbe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 25 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5361e7974d96db803e913bba80f779505beb54a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 32$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Using this same <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> value, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd780617b560570d536df8c10c0968c58740491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />, like in solution 1.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.2\">Solution 1.2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can repeat the same steps at first from solution 1 or solution 1.1. However, instead of plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> into the first equation, we can also plug it into the second equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/1033ded929aa293b239d804107992ca65f578bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(50 - 32)^{2} + h^{2} = 30^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d701bbda33bb9d50764da9eb56aa360d1813cf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18^{2} + h^{2} = 30^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb42ab9521705425930b2df26d9363aeb829c954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^{2} = 30^{2} - 18^{2} = 12  \\times 48 = 12^{2} \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c80ba656cb6cf617a406beaa66c6a9328cab3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 12 \\times \\sqrt{4} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28similar_triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(similar_triangles)\">Solution 2 (similar triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (similar triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can draw the same triangle as in solution 1, and let CD be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>However, we see that we have similar triangles because of equal angles:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/5180fa5b749def6ce4838afaec5abcd53d15cae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h}{30} = \\frac{40}{50} = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfdf65fa70bba8636c3033f6959c075067c4deeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 30 \\times \\frac{4}{5} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"179\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28official_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(official_solution)\">Solution 3 (official solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (official solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can draw the triangle and its altitude and mark it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can notice that the triangle has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74aa1fbc1fb48b46f827d82f65fbf3cb90c82012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 \\times 40 = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89a79dcf79ee59948473d3a9694d645d5d3ca3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times h \\times 50 = 25h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" /> also represents the area of the triangle, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4abb5c53c99fcfb28e99699946bfc98371a81f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25h = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/5162f30bb008ff6a215416a69e01060550998cab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 600 \\div 25 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"193\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~solution by CEMC Gauss modified by anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"199